# Everything here is excluded from the build context. This matters for speed as
# much as correctness: public/ alone is ~150MB of video, and node_modules is
# larger still — without this file every `docker build` uploads all of it to the
# daemon before the first instruction runs.

# Reinstalled inside the image by `npm ci`. Copying the host's copy would also
# drag in platform-specific binaries built for Windows.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build artefacts — the image produces its own.
build
dist
coverage

# VCS + editor
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
*.swp

# Secrets. The image needs REACT_APP_* as BUILD ARGS, not as a baked-in file;
# copying .env here would embed whatever the developer had locally into the
# image and make builds non-reproducible across machines.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Docker's own files — no reason to send them into the context.
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml

# Logs / OS noise
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local scratch
*.crdownload
README.md
